y at Kael's sabotage of supplies, want to use the chart in the Toll War, which would expose Maris's smuggling routes.","outcome":"Veya and Maris quarrel over whether to publish, and Maris leaves, feeling betrayed.","summary":"At Emberroost, the Wardens press Veya to publish. Maris sees her routes at risk, and the alliance breaks over secrecy versus truth.","depends_on":["scn_the_chart_is_stolen"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Breaking Point","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_kael_moves_on_the_hollow","title":"Kael Seizes the Silos","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to seize the grain and end the smuggling, and Maris wants to protect The Hollow's last stock.","conflict":"Kael's enforcers hold the silos, and Maris must choose between hiding to survive and standing against him.","outcome":"Maris stalls him long enough to hide the last grain, but Kael learns Veya's charts are what made the runs possible.","summary":"Kael arrives in The Hollow with enforcers and takes the silos. Maris holds him off and saves the last stock, and he learns who helped her.","depends_on":["scn_wardens_demand_answers"]},{"id":"scn_veya_and_maris_reunite","title":"Choosing Each Other","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to publish the chart, and Maris wants to save The Hollow, so they must agree on a shared plan.","conflict":"Veya must admit she was wrong to hoard the chart, and Maris must forgive her and trust her again.","outcome":"Veya admits her mistake, and Maris agrees to publish the chart with the grain routes folded into it as a lifeline for every isle.","summary":"Maris brings Veya the news of Kael's raid. Veya admits she was wrong, and they decide to publish the truth together.","depends_on":["scn_kael_moves_on_the_hollow"]},{"id":"scn_the_final_confrontation","title":"The Grain and the Map","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want to publish the chart and distribute the grain publicly, while Kael wants to stop them and keep the peace.","conflict":"Kael threatens to cut the cable of the docks and sever the routes, which would destroy both the chart's purpose and the grain's path.","outcome":"Veya reads the currents and shows the crowd the bridges are failing, and Kael, seeing control would cost more than it gains, stands down.","summary":"On the docks, Kael moves to destroy both the chart and the grain. Veya's public reading and Maris's open shipment turn the crowd against him, and he yields.","depends_on":["scn_veya_and_maris_reunite"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What Remains","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_the_charts_are_shared","title":"Truth Shared","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the chart copied and shared with every isle, and Maris wants a safe route for grain.","conflict":"Some Academy scholars resist, and Veya must accept credit shared with Maris and the Wardens rather than keep it herself.","outcome":"The chart is distributed openly, and Veya accepts shared credit, letting go of her need for sole recognition.","summary":"Veya and Maris copy the chart for every isle. Veya shares credit, and the safe routes carry the grain to those in need.","depends_on":["scn_the_final_confrontation"]},{"id":"scn_kael_pays_the_price","title":"The Cost of Control","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to repair his standing and the Cartel's, and Veya wants the Wardens and the Cartel to share the bridges.","conflict":"Kael's pride and his belief that price equals worth fight against what he has learned about the cost of control.","outcome":"Kael agrees to fund bridge repairs instead of tolls, and he and Veya begin a wary peace.","summary":"At the forge, Kael meets Veya and the Wardens, and he accepts that control cost him more than it gained. He pays for repairs and the rivals begin a wary peace.","depends_on":["scn_the_final_confrontation","scn_the_charts_are_shared"]},{"id":"scn_the_hollow_harvest","title":"Windmills Turning","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Maris wants to see The Hollow fed and the levy lifted, and the others want to witness the new arrangement hold.","conflict":"Maris must decide whether she can forgive Kael and trust the new peace, given her flaw of rarely forgiving.","outcome":"The levy is replaced by a fair exchange, and Maris accepts that quiet work can be as brave as open defiance.","summary":"The windmills of The Hollow turn again under the new terms. Maris watches the grain go out openly and finds peace in the work she did in hiding.","depends_on":["scn_kael_pays_the_price"]}]}]}
