s","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want to publish the chart and distribute the grain publicly, while Kael wants to stop them and keep the peace.","conflict":"Kael threatens to cut the cable of the docks and sever the routes, which would destroy both the chart's purpose and the grain's path.","outcome":"Veya reads the currents and shows the crowd the bridges are failing, and Kael, seeing control would cost more than it gains, stands down.","summary":"On the docks, Kael moves to destroy both the chart and the grain. Veya's public reading and Maris's open shipment turn the crowd against him, and he yields.","depends_on":["scn_veya_and_maris_reunite"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What Remains","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_the_charts_are_shared","title":"Truth Shared","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the chart copied and shared with every isle, and Maris wants a safe route for grain.","conflict":"Some Academy scholars resist, and Veya must accept credit shared with Maris and the Wardens rather than keep it herself.","outcome":"The chart is distributed openly, and Veya accepts shared credit, letting go of her need for sole recognition.","summary":"Veya and Maris copy the chart for every isle. Veya shares credit, and the safe routes carry the grain to those in need.","depends_on":["scn_the_final_confrontation"]},{"id":"scn_kael_pays_the_price","title":"The Cost of Control","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to repair his standing and the Cartel's, and Veya wants the Wardens and the Cartel to share the bridges.","conflict":"Kael's pride and his belief that price equals worth fight against what he has learned about the cost of control.","outcome":"Kael agrees to fund bridge repairs instead of tolls, and he and Veya begin a wary peace.","summary":"At the forge, Kael meets Veya and the Wardens, and he accepts that control cost him more than