{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Grain and the Map","logline":"When Veya's charts reveal the skybridges are failing and Maris's smuggled grain becomes the only thing feeding The Hollow, Kael moves to destroy both to protect the Cartel's monopoly and his fragile peace, forcing the three to decide whether truth, loyalty, or control is worth the cost.","theme":"Some truths are safer shared than hoarded.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"Charts and Secrets","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_veya_charts_the_fade","title":"The Fading Bridges","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants to confirm with her wind-sight that the skybridge network is breaking and that her late mentor's theory is right.","conflict":"The readings contradict the Academy's official charts, and Veya's stubbornness makes her hide the data until she is certain rather than raise the alarm.","outcome":"She completes a draft chart showing the safest remaining routes and the isles drifting apart, and decides to keep it private for now.","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya reads the colours of the wind and sees the bridges failing faster than anyone admits. She draws a new chart and tells no one."},{"id":"scn_maris_counts_the_levy","title":"The Levy Comes Due","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Maris wants to hide enough grain from the Cartel levy to keep The Hollow fed.","conflict":"Cartel enforcers are tallying the silos, and Maris trusts too few people to ask for help.","outcome":"She moves a first hidden stock through the unmapped service corridors, but an enforcer notices discrepancies in the count.","summary":"Maris uses her knowledge of the windmill corridors to shift grain out of sight while the Cartel counts the silos. The tally comes up short, and suspicion falls on The Hollow."},{"id":"scn_kael_hears_of_the_charts","title":"A Toll-Master's Ledger","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to secure the last stable skybridge routes for the Cartel before the bridges collapse.","conflict":"Rumours reach him of a new chart from Silverspine, and the Wardens accuse him of sabotaging forge-island supplies, which he cannot publicly answer.","outcome":"Kael resolves to obtain Veya's charts and learns the grain tally from The Hollow is short, so he decides to watch both.","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael reads his ledgers and sees the pressure from both the Wardens and the grain levy. Word of Veya's chart and The Hollow's missing grain tells him two threats are rising together.","depends_on":["scn_veya_charts_the_fade","scn_maris_counts_the_levy"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Closing Nets","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_veya_meets_maris","title":"Trading Paths","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants a safe route to test her charts, and Maris wants wind-current knowledge to move grain safely.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and suspects Veya's motives, while Veya refuses to share the full chart.","outcome":"They agree to an exchange: Veya reads the currents for Maris's routes, and Maris opens her service corridors to Veya.","summary":"Veya travels to The Hollow and bargains with Maris. Wary on both sides, they trade current-reading for secret paths and form a fragile alliance.","depends_on":["scn_veya_charts_the_fade","scn_maris_counts_the_levy"]},{"id":"scn_kael_offers_veya_a_deal","title":"An Old Rival's Offer","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants Veya's charts for the Cartel, and Veya wants to learn how much Kael already knows.","conflict":"Kael's charm and his admiration for her work clash with Veya's refusal to let him control the charts, and her pride keeps her from admitting the danger.","outcome":"Veya refuses the offer and leaves, and Kael understands she will not sell, so he orders enforcers to watch her.","summary":"Kael meets his old fellow apprentice on the docks and offers her a seat in the Cartel. Veya declines, and Kael decides charm will not be enough.","depends_on":["scn_kael_hears_of_the_charts","scn_veya_meets_maris"]},{"id":"scn_the_first_run","title":"Grain Through the Corridors","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Smuggle a first large grain shipment out through the windmill corridors without being seen by the enforcers.","conflict":"Enforcers close in on the usual routes, and Maris must rely on Veya's wind-sight, which forces her to trust an outsider.","outcome":"The shipment gets through on Veya's reading of the currents, and Maris begins to trust Veya, though an enforcer sees them.","summary":"With Veya reading the wind and Maris leading through the corridors, they slip grain past the enforcers. The success deepens their bond and exposes them to Kael.","depends_on":["scn_veya_meets_maris","scn_kael_offers_veya_a_deal"]},{"id":"scn_the_chart_is_stolen","title":"The Archive Breach","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants to retrieve and protect her draft chart and the mentor's notes that prove the isles are drifting apart.","conflict":"The Cartel has pressured the Academy to bury the findings, and Veya's refusal to admit her own carelessness blocks her from seeking Wardens' help.","outcome":"She saves only a partial copy, and she realises that keeping the truth to herself has left her exposed.","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine and finds her work disturbed on Kael's orders. She salvages part of it and begins to doubt her secrecy.","depends_on":["scn_kael_offers_veya_a_deal","scn_the_first_run"]},{"id":"scn_wardens_demand_answers","title":"The Forge Accusation","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the Bridge Wardens to help publish the chart, and Maris wants to keep the grain routes secret.","conflict":"The Wardens, angry at Kael's sabotage of supplies, want to use the chart in the Toll War, which would expose Maris's smuggling routes.","outcome":"Veya and Maris quarrel over whether to publish, and Maris leaves, feeling betrayed.","summary":"At Emberroost, the Wardens press Veya to publish. Maris sees her routes at risk, and the alliance breaks over secrecy versus truth.","depends_on":["scn_the_chart_is_stolen"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Breaking Point","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_kael_moves_on_the_hollow","title":"Kael Seizes the Silos","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to seize the grain and end the smuggling, and Maris wants to protect The Hollow's last stock.","conflict":"Kael's enforcers hold the silos, and Maris must choose between hiding to survive and standing against him.","outcome":"Maris stalls him long enough to hide the last grain, but Kael learns Veya's charts are what made the runs possible.","summary":"Kael arrives in The Hollow with enforcers and takes the silos. Maris holds him off and saves the last stock, and he learns who helped her.","depends_on":["scn_wardens_demand_answers"]},{"id":"scn_veya_and_maris_reunite","title":"Choosing Each Other","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to publish the chart, and Maris wants to save The Hollow, so they must agree on a shared plan.","conflict":"Veya must admit she was wrong to hoard the chart, and Maris must forgive her and trust her again.","outcome":"Veya admits her mistake, and Maris agrees to publish the chart with the grain routes folded into it as a lifeline for every isle.","summary":"Maris brings Veya the news of Kael's raid. Veya admits she was wrong, and they decide to publish the truth together.","depends_on":["scn_kael_moves_on_the_hollow"]},{"id":"scn_the_final_confrontation","title":"The Grain and the Map","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want to publish the chart and distribute the grain publicly, while Kael wants to stop them and keep the peace.","conflict":"Kael threatens to cut the cable of the docks and sever the routes, which would destroy both the chart's purpose and the grain's path.","outcome":"Veya reads the currents and shows the crowd the bridges are failing, and Kael, seeing control would cost more than it gains, stands down.","summary":"On the docks, Kael moves to destroy both the chart and the grain. Veya's public reading and Maris's open shipment turn the crowd against him, and he yields.","depends_on":["scn_veya_and_maris_reunite"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What Remains","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_the_charts_are_shared","title":"Truth Shared","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the chart copied and shared with every isle, and Maris wants a safe route for grain.","conflict":"Some Academy scholars resist, and Veya must accept credit shared with Maris and the Wardens rather than keep it herself.","outcome":"The chart is distributed openly, and Veya accepts shared credit, letting go of her need for sole recognition.","summary":"Veya and Maris copy the chart for every isle. Veya shares credit, and the safe routes carry the grain to those in need.","depends_on":["scn_the_final_confrontation"]},{"id":"scn_kael_pays_the_price","title":"The Cost of Control","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to repair his standing and the Cartel's, and Veya wants the Wardens and the Cartel to share the bridges.","conflict":"Kael's pride and his belief that price equals worth fight against what he has learned about the cost of control.","outcome":"Kael agrees to fund bridge repairs instead of tolls, and he and Veya begin a wary peace.","summary":"At the forge, Kael meets Veya and the Wardens, and he accepts that control cost him more than it gained. He pays for repairs and the rivals begin a wary peace.","depends_on":["scn_the_final_confrontation","scn_the_charts_are_shared"]},{"id":"scn_the_hollow_harvest","title":"Windmills Turning","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Maris wants to see The Hollow fed and the levy lifted, and the others want to witness the new arrangement hold.","conflict":"Maris must decide whether she can forgive Kael and trust the new peace, given her flaw of rarely forgiving.","outcome":"The levy is replaced by a fair exchange, and Maris accepts that quiet work can be as brave as open defiance.","summary":"The windmills of The Hollow turn again under the new terms. Maris watches the grain go out openly and finds peace in the work she did in hiding.","depends_on":["scn_kael_pays_the_price"]}]}]}
